{"seconds": 44.3, "exit": 0, "final": "Qxf6+ just trades a queen for a pawn and rook, losing material. Qe7+ is clearly superior as it threatens to win the rook without giving up the queen.\n\nThe move is **Qe7+** and it wins material (the rook on f8) because:\n1. It checks the king, forcing it to move\n2. All king moves leave the rook on f8 undefended\n3. All defensive tries (Rf7, Qxe7) lose the rook or queen\n\n**Best move: Qe7+**\n\n**Main line:** Qe7+ Kh8 (or Kg8/Kh6) Qxf8+\n\n**Motif: deflection** (or also could be called \"attraction\" - forcing the king away from defending the rook)\n\n**Coaching note:** When you have a powerful queen like White's on e6, look for checks that also attack enemy pieces on the back rank. Here, Qe7+ simultaneously checks the king AND attacks the undefended rook on f8. After the king moves, the rook falls. This is a key pattern: forcing moves that win material because they uncover or isolate a piece from protection.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qe7+\", \"line\": [\"Qe7+\", \"Kh8\", \"Qxf8+\", \"Kh7\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27", "square": "a3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27", "square": "c3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27", "square": "f8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27", "square": "e6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "5r2/6k1/p3Qpp1/1p5p/3P4/q1r4R/5PPP/4R1K1 w - - 0 27", "square": "h3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-